#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial is inspired by and based upon research conducted at Cleveland Clinic, as described in [Kaliakin, Danil, et al. \"Implicit solvent sample-based quantum diagonalization.\" The Journal of Physical Chemistry B 129.23 (2025): 5788-5796](https://pubs.acs.org/doi/10.1021/acs.jpcb.5c01030), exposing the full workflow for implicit solvent calculations and extending it with iterative solvent self-consistency (\"The Heartwood Algorithm\", M. Motta, T. Pellegrini, 2025), geometry optimization, and automatic qubit layout selection. Please refer to the [SQD IEF-PCM Qiskit Function template](/guides/function-template-chemistry-workflow), jointly developed by Cleveland Clinic and IBM&reg; based on Cleveland Clinic research, for a streamlined, black-box interface for running implicit solvent calculations.\n"
msgstr "Ang tutorial na ito ay inspirasyon at batay sa pananaliksik na isinagawa sa Cleveland Clinic, gaya ng inilarawan sa [Kaliakin, Danil, et al. \"Implicit solvent sample-based quantum diagonalization.\" The Journal of Physical Chemistry B 129.23 (2025): 5788-5796](https://pubs.acs.org/doi/10.1021/acs.jpcb.5c01030), na inilalantad ang buong workflow para sa implicit solvent calculations at pinapalawak ito gamit ang iterative solvent self-consistency (\"The Heartwood Algorithm\", M. Motta, T. Pellegrini, 2025), geometry optimization, at automatic qubit layout selection. Mangyaring sumangguni sa [SQD IEF-PCM Qiskit Function template](/guides/function-template-chemistry-workflow), na magkasamang binuo ng Cleveland Clinic at IBM&reg; batay sa pananaliksik ng Cleveland Clinic, para sa isang streamlined, black-box interface sa pagpapatakbo ng implicit solvent calculations.\n"

